course: dictionary
lesson: 13662
title: Words that change things
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Influential means having a lot of influence: able to change what other people think or do, or how things happen. Look inside the word: influence is the power to change things, and influential describes someone or something that has that power. «Her kind words were influential, and soon the whole class was helping each other.» Her words changed what the class did.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «The book was influential in changing how children learned to read.» The book made a big difference to how children learned, so influential means it had a strong effect. Notice the little word in: influential in, as in «He was influential in starting the school garden.»
explain: Check your meaning by swapping in a simpler word. Try powerful or important in the sentence: «She is an important person» still fits, so you are on the right track. Influential is more exact, though. It means something changed because of you, your ideas or your actions.
fact: Influential means able to change what other people think or do, or how things happen.
fact: «An influential person» is someone whose ideas or actions make a big difference to other people.
fact: Influence is the noun; influential is the adjective. You can compare it: influential, more influential, most influential.
fact: Useful phrases: «highly influential», «influential in», and «an influential idea».
fact: A good check is to swap in powerful or important and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «Our coach was an influential person, and the whole team began to play with more care.» What does influential mean? | Loud and cheerful | *Able to change what other people think or do | Very tired after training | Old and slow
exercise: «The book was influential in changing how children learned to read.» What did the book do? | Sold very cheaply | Was hard to read | *Changed how children learned | Made nothing change
exercise: Which word is closest in meaning to influential? | Quiet | Tiny | *Powerful | Ordinary
test: «She is the most influential writer in our class.» What does most influential show? | The writer is the newest in the class | The writer is the shortest | The writer writes the most pages | *The writer has the greatest effect on what others think or do
test: Ben says, «That idea was highly influential.» What does Ben mean? | The idea was very boring | *The idea had a big effect on people or on how things happened | The idea was lost | The idea was hard to understand
exam: Which sentence uses influential correctly? | *The scientist was influential, and her discovery changed how doctors treat illness. | The biscuit was influential and tasted of lemon. | The dog was influential in running very fast on the grass. | The rain was influential, so we stayed indoors and read.
